        "<div style=\"border-left: 5px solid #4B2E83; background-color: #F9F7FC; padding: 20px 25px; margin: 20px 0; border-radius: 5px;\">\n",
        "  <h2 style=\"color: #4B2E83; font-family: 'Encode Sans', 'Arial', sans-serif; margin-top: 0;\">3.1 Bar Plot</h2>\n",
        "</div>\n",
        "\n",
        "**What it is:** A bar plot displays categorical data with rectangular bars whose lengths are proportional to the values they represent.\n",
        "\n",
        "**How to read it:** Each bar corresponds to a category. Compare bar heights (or lengths) to judge relative magnitudes.\n",
        "\n",
        "**When to use it:** When you have a *categorical* (or ordinal) variable and want to compare counts, proportions, or aggregated values across categories.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Titanic application:** Compare the survival rate across passenger classes."
      ],
      "id": "5689223699624ac4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "ExecuteTime": {
          "end_time": "2026-04-03T16:13:39.204187Z",
