        "**How to read it:** Position encodes two variables (x, y); bubble area encodes a third. Larger bubbles represent higher values of the size variable.\n",
        "\n",
        "**When to use it:** When you want to show relationships among *three* (or four) variables simultaneously.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Titanic application:** Each bubble is an (Age group, Class) combination; size represents number of passengers; colour represents survival rate."
